 ```{dropdown} Explanation
-Zero is a valid amount, not a recognition flag. An unknown code needs an explicit invalid branch, or a separate Boolean recording whether any supported case matched. Only a recognized code may produce the corresponding service report. A `switch` default can reject the code before printing a charge; an `if` chain can use a final invalid branch. Neither repair needs a loop or a user-defined method.
+An amount records a price, not which branch matched. Before repair, `P` explicitly assigns zero while `X` matches no case and retains the initial zero. After repair, `default` rejects `X` and returns before the price-based report. With these three recognized services, only pickup reaches that report with zero. Tab 4 adds free standard delivery, so it reports the recognized service explicitly instead of treating every zero as pickup.
